1. palantir-java-format  (Apache License 2.0)
================================================================================

Location in this repository: hyperion-fmt/src/doc/

    break_.rs, compute.rs, indent.rs, level.rs, mod.rs, render.rs, state.rs,
    tests.rs

Upstream:   https://github.com/palantir/palantir-java-format
Copyright:  Palantir Technologies Inc.
License:    Apache License, Version 2.0

palantir-java-format is itself a derivative of google-java-format:

Upstream:   https://github.com/google/google-java-format
Copyright:  Google LLC
License:    Apache License, Version 2.0

The `hyperion-fmt::doc` module is a Rust port of the backtracking layout solver
of palantir-java-format -- principally the classes

    com.palantir.javaformat.doc.Doc
    com.palantir.javaformat.doc.Level
    com.palantir.javaformat.doc.Break
    com.palantir.javaformat.doc.BreakTag
    com.palantir.javaformat.doc.FillMode
    com.palantir.javaformat.doc.State
    com.palantir.javaformat.Indent
    com.palantir.javaformat.OpenOp
    com.palantir.javaformat.BreakBehaviour
    com.palantir.javaformat.LastLevelBreakability
    com.palantir.javaformat.PartialInlineability

and the pending-indent output discipline of

    com.palantir.javaformat.java.JavaOutput

The port has been modified from the original: it is a translation into Rust, it
substitutes persistent `im` collections keyed by integer ids for the reference's
identity-keyed functional-java maps, it collapses the reference's `Obs`
exploration harness into plain functions, and it restricts `Indent::If` branches
to constants. The individual source files name the classes they derive from.

The remainder of hyperion-fmt is original work. It emulates the *output style*
of palantir-java-format but is not derived from its source.

